WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.417
(rock music)

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.230
- Me and Annie are gonna
try Singaporean McDonalds

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.860
for the very first time.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.900
We didn't know what to order,

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.780
so we asked our friends over here,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.613
Sylvia and Aiken.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:14.710
- Hola

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.265
- So I think you should
try the Nasi Lemak burger.

00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:19.280
This is basically
everything a Nasi Lemak is,

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.408
but without the rice.

00:00:20.408 --> 00:00:21.241
- Oh, that's true.

00:00:21.241 --> 00:00:23.440
- I'm gonna show you the
inside, which is beautiful.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.420
- [Annie] Whoa! Do you see that steam?

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.633
- I actually, I'm a little worried. Ready?

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:32.972
It's actually really good.

00:00:32.972 --> 00:00:34.210
Kind of confusing though.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.933
- It's like slightly sour, which I like.

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:37.240
- It's the sauce, right?

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.210
What do you call that sauce?

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.043
- [Aiken] Sambal.

00:00:39.043 --> 00:00:39.950
- Sambal Belacan.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.270
Sambal Belacan basically is like

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.020
a very Asian tasting chili.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.440
- It's so juicy. That's insane.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.670
I think the best part of this is the egg.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.433
- Yeah. Cucumber in a
burger is weird though.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.740
- Our McSpicy is the best in the region

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.470
because it is the spiciest.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.303
- [Annie] Oh no.

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:57.300
- We heard from our friends over here

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.030
that the spiciness can have an impact

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.750
on your digestive system in a strong way.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.750
- Why do they feel so substantial here?

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.849
Like it kinda looks like
the promotional pictures.

00:01:07.849 --> 00:01:10.030
(chuckles)

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.244
- Okay, you guys hyped
this up too much for me.

00:01:12.244 --> 00:01:13.900
It's not that spicy.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.070
- My tongue's on fire.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.840
- Really? Does it get worse?

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.310
Yeah. It took like 20 seconds
to start feeling the spice.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.580
Yeah. It's pretty good.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.490
- It has a lot of flavor.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.352
- I will, I'll tell you
tomorrow on how powerful

00:01:25.352 --> 00:01:27.360
this dish was to my system.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.820
- Maybe you shouldn't.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.310
- Wait. Ice cream break.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:32.110
There's a little hack,
apparently, here in Singapore.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.640
If you order a McDelivery,
you order ice cream

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.260
so that they'll deliver
it to you faster, hmm.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.610
Oh, that tastes exactly like the American

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.862
soft serve version.

00:01:41.862 --> 00:01:44.070
(guitar music)

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.400
- There's nothing in the world like this.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.600
- Very unique.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.740
- Now I'm scared.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.986
Today we go for the hot curry sauce.

00:01:50.986 --> 00:01:53.820
Oh! That is a color.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.120
- It does look like curry.

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:00.970
It's not bad.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.040
- It's like sweet and sour
mixed with a curry powder

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.090
and it has an interesting aftertaste.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.250
- It probably isn't my sauce of choice.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.080
- Oh, my god. Where my Singaporeans at?

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.104
Steve and Annie don't like
curry sauce lah. (gasps)

00:02:16.104 --> 00:02:18.210
(laughter)

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.200
We have the cheesy fries,
which is new in our menu

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.150
in our country.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.047
I hope it's good.

00:02:23.047 --> 00:02:25.230
(laughter)

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.150
- It looks a little wimpy.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.170
Okay, let's just do this.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.300
When you eat fries at McDonald's,

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.660
you gotta eat like 10 at a time.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.493
- Oh.

00:02:32.493 --> 00:02:33.490
- [Steven] Oh.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.504
- [Annie] Perfect.

00:02:34.504 --> 00:02:35.337
- Mmm.

00:02:35.337 --> 00:02:36.170
- But it's good.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.003
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:37.003 --> 00:02:38.262
It's something you would
get at a hot dog stand.

00:02:38.262 --> 00:02:39.950
- It does taste like a hot dog.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.600
- The fries are the exact
same as they are in America.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.820
You can't really go wrong
when you have cheese, bacon.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.030
How can you mess that up?

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:49.690
I wanna see what they
think for the first time.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.634
- Well, it's quite nice.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:51.467
- Mm.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.912
- Right, ordinarily, you
would just eat this part

00:02:53.912 --> 00:02:56.950
and they wouldn't do with
the rest that has nothing.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.400
- I did not know what to expect.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.540
I thought it would be the same.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.760
It actually was better to do here.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.712
- Everything had a
slight Asian flair to it.

00:03:03.712 --> 00:03:06.432
- An Asian flair in an actually Asian way.

00:03:06.432 --> 00:03:07.265
Mm.

00:03:07.265 --> 00:03:11.432
(upbeat guitar and violin music)

